<title>BELGIUM: Fortis eyes parent wedding.</title>
<headline>Fortis eyes parent wedding.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A full merger of the parent companies of Belgian-Dutch banking and insurance group Fortis will happen the day it proves &quot;useful and necessary&quot;, the chairman of Belgian Fortis AG said on Friday.</p>
<p>Fortis AG jointly controls Fortis along with Fortis AMEV of the Netherlands.</p>
<p>&quot;We are heading to a situation where the two parent companies have no other assets but their parts in the group. We are heading towards a merger, but we are not in a hurry,&quot; AG chairman Maurice Lippens told Belgian financial newspaper L'Echo in an interview.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
